<title>FRANCE: STRIKING GIAT WORKERS RELEASE HOSTAGE DIRECTOR.</title>
<headline>STRIKING GIAT WORKERS RELEASE HOSTAGE DIRECTOR.</headline>
<dateline>TOULOUSE, France 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Striking workers at arms maker GIAT-Industries in Tarbes released their plant director, Daniel Girardot, after having taken him hostage as part of a protest against planned lay-offs.</p>
<p>Daniel Ploton, spokesman for the protestors, said they had left Girardot's office in the afternoon and the director had been able to &quot;continue normally his professional activities&quot;.</p>
<p>Some 90 percent of the plant's workers had downed tools earlier on Thursday and resumed work in the afternoon. The Tarbes plant in southwestern France makes parts for the Leclerc tank.</p>
</text>
